Port of LinuxOnTab commit 7b5cb89 ("fix: hush NOMMU pipe hang") to busybox
source. The fix was originally applied only to the prebuilt wasm binary in
rootfs/bin/busybox; this makes it a source patch so rebuilds keep it.

run_pipe() passed &pipefds.rd (always 0 on the first iteration) as the stdin
fd for the first pipe command, so its stdin was the pipe read end instead of
the terminal. Pass &next_infd instead, which starts at 0 (terminal) and is
updated to the previous pipe's read end between iterations.

--- a/shell/hush.c
+++ b/shell/hush.c
@@ -9791,7 +9791,7 @@
         args.nommu_save = &nommu_save;
 #endif
         args.pipefds = &pipefds;
-        args.next_infd = &pipefds.rd;
+        args.next_infd = &next_infd;
 		command->pid = clone(run_pipe_child, child_stack, CLONE_VM | CLONE_VFORK | SIGCHLD, &args);

 		/* parent or error */
